      <div num="p-0041" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. 21</figref> shows SEM images for the structure of pores present in each polyethylene matrix after each of the following blends is cooled to a temperature less than or equivalent to a crystallization temperature of polyethylene: (a) a blend of polyethylene//(poly(tetramethylene ether) glycol (650)/soybean oil=5/95)=20//80, (b) a blend of polyethylene//(poly(tetramethylene ether) glycol (650)/soybean oil=5/95)=30//70, and (c) a blend of polyethylene//(poly(tetramethylene ether) glycol (650)/soybean oil=5/95)=40//60.</div>
